[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   step_17: the planetary baseline -- the test the whole analysis needed.
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   Every earlier test compared raw d_of against the axis.  The correct
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   TEP observable is the residual AFTER the standard planetary baseline.
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   This step builds that baseline:
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   For each comet: node heliocentric distances r_asc, r_desc (analytic
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   from q, e, w) and Jupiter's ecliptic longitude at the perihelion
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   epoch (mean longitude 34.35 deg at J2000, rate 30.349 deg/yr --
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   an analytic approximation adequate for a covariance baseline).
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   Encounter proxy jproxy = min over nodes of the combined
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   node-distance/node-timing separation (a comet is perturbed
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   strongly only when a node sits near 5.2 AU AND Jupiter is there).
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   Baseline regression: log(d_of) ~ 1 + jproxy + q over the full
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   sample -> residuals.  Then the axis tests run on the residuals:
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   cap contrast and the continuous Spearman test, no cap, no cuts.
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   The baseline works: d_of correlates with jproxy globally
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   (rho = -0.47).  The in-cap comets carry NO geometric advantage
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   (jproxy, node_min, i, q, |daa| all flat vs out-cap).  And the
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   residual axis preference STRENGTHENS: p = 0.0018 (matched),
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   p = 0.0036 cap / rho = -0.28, p = 0.0012 continuous (all class-1).
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   Standard planetary geometry is now explicitly subtracted; what
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   remains is the non-planetary residual, and it still points at
[2026-09-21 14:36:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 040]   the TNO axis.
